C/ DB id 34 (no_return_function_undefined_behavior_diverges): a
C/ FUNCTION with no RETURN statement, once called, must be detected as
C/ USA003090 Appendix C error #14 (NO RETURN STATEMENT IN FUNCTION)
C/ and given a deterministic, type-appropriate default per the
C/ manual's own documented "Continue" fixup -- confirmed against real
C/ gpc that the error IS genuinely detected/logged (its own fallback
C/ value is real hardware register leftovers, not a spec-defined
C/ target, so not reproduced here).

  T:
  PROGRAM;
     DECLARE R SCALAR;
  NORET:
  FUNCTION SCALAR;
     DECLARE S SCALAR;
     S = 5;
  CLOSE NORET;
     R = NORET;
     WRITE(6) 'R=', R;
     WRITE(6) 'ERRGRP=', ERRGRP;
     WRITE(6) 'ERRNUM=', ERRNUM;
Y %SVCI(0);
  CLOSE T;
